About:

This directory contains a number of source files modified to duplicate Oscar Agertz's Ramses patch shared by him with me and fully self-contained in:

/Users/tepper/codes/ramses_agertz/ramses

The idea is to merge his changes with the most updated Ramses version and keep it that way as Ramses evolves.

Note that the sub-folder 'dice' contains its own README and is thus omitted here.

The file filesf90_list.txt (created with ls *f90) contains a list of the files in here less sub-directories and their content, created for convenience in case they need to be recopied from the main branch or O.Agertz's patch.

NOTE:
	Instructions from Oscar Agertz himself to include his changes:

	"
		the only thing we want which is different from the master branch is:

		1) The DICE loader
		2) feedback.f90, with the relevant parameters added to amr_parameters.f90, read_hydro.f90 and read_hydro_parameters.f90.
		3) The fact that we have more variables for star particles than in standard RAMSES, specifically
			mpb: birth mass of particles
			zp: metals.
		The treatment of extra star variables entail minor modifications to files like the output_part.f90, init_part.f90, particle_tree.f90 and a couple of others (easily identifiable by grepping for mpb and zp, EDGE, or ERIC within the *f90 source files).

		The rest of the changes made relate to things like particle tracers, compatibility with the genetIC code, a new movie routine used for zoom simulations with automatic particle centering. We don’t need this and a new patch for our project can leave them out.
	"

IMPORTANT:

	- File read_params.f90 from /Users/tepper/codes/ramses_agertz/ramses/amr IS MISSING!!!!
		- S*unit_out are not defined if SNdiagnostics = .false.

	!!!! FIX the above!!!


	- units.f90 has been renamed so that it is not longer compiled and overriden by tepper/amr/units.f90. Note that this change MUST be accompanied by including the following block in the NML file (also when running Oscar's original setup!)

	&UNITS_PARAMS
	units_density = 1.573391528d-26			! g/cm^3 = 1 H / cm^3
	units_time    = 3.00386047142391D+15 	! s; irrelevant if poisson=.true.
	units_length  = 3.0856776D+21 			! cm = 1 kpc
	/

	- feedback.f90 has been copied directly, as it seemed OK to do so

	- condinit.f90 has been copied directly

	- metal_yields.f90 does not exist in the current Ramses version and has been copied directly; note that this requires an appropriate Makefile:

	/Users/tepper/codes/ramses_fork/bin/Makefile_3D_GNU_OLDMPI0_OAgertz

	which also contains other modifications wrt my standard Makefiles, e.g. NMETALS = 2, etc.

	Note that metal_yields.f90 may in fact not be needed (ask Oscar!)
